input.findings:
## Summary of the bug

`src/theme/dark.ts` has a `matrix` block whose keys do NOT match `MatrixOption`. Two of the three entries are dead options, and the body/corner cells + divider lines are never themed at all, so in dark mode they keep the light-mode token values baked into `MatrixModel`'s `defaultOption` (dark-gray label text on a near-black background, light-gray cell borders).

## Where matrix defaults come from (read-only reference, no edits needed)

`src/coord/matrix/MatrixModel.ts` (the view is at `src/component/matrix/MatrixView.ts`, not `src/coord/matrix/`):

- MatrixModel.ts:215-224 — label default, used by x, y, body AND corner:
```ts
const defaultLabelOption: LabelOption = {
    show: true,
    color: tokens.color.secondary,
```
- MatrixModel.ts:225-231 — cell border default:
```ts
function makeDefaultCellItemStyleOption(isCorner: boolean) {
    return {
        color: 'none',
        borderWidth: 1,
        borderColor: isCorner ? 'none' : tokens.color.borderTint,
    };
};
```
- MatrixModel.ts:232-241 — divider line default (applies to `matrix.x` and `matrix.y`, both use the same `defaultDimOption` object):
```ts
const defaultDimOption: MatrixDimensionOption = {
    show: true,
    label: defaultLabelOption,
    itemStyle: makeDefaultCellItemStyleOption(false),
    silent: undefined,
    dividerLineStyle: {
        width: 1,
        color: tokens.color.border,
    },
};
```
- MatrixModel.ts:242-251 — `defaultBodyOption` uses `makeDefaultCellItemStyleOption(false)`, `defaultCornerOption` uses `makeDefaultCellItemStyleOption(true)` (i.e. corner border is `'none'`).
- MatrixModel.ts:252-269 — overall background / outer border:
```ts
    backgroundStyle: {
        color: 'none',
        borderColor: tokens.color.axisLine,
        borderWidth: 1,
    },
```
So the four themeable colors are: `matrix.x/y/body/corner.label.color` (= `tokens.color.secondary`), `matrix.x/y/body.itemStyle.borderColor` (= `tokens.color.borderTint`; corner is `'none'`), `matrix.x/y.dividerLineStyle.color` (= `tokens.color.border`), `matrix.backgroundStyle.borderColor` (= `tokens.color.axisLine`).

Consumers, for confirmation: `src/component/matrix/MatrixView.ts:90-99` reads `matrixModel.getModel('backgroundStyle')` twice (fill rect + outer border rect); MatrixView.ts:117 / :129 read `xDimModel/yDimModel.getModel('dividerLineStyle').getLineStyle()`; MatrixView.ts:198-200 builds body/corner style models from `matrixModel.getShallow('body'|'corner', true)` — note `ignoreParent: true`, so a color set at `matrix.label`/`matrix.itemStyle` root would NOT reach body/corner; the theme must set each branch (`x`, `y`, `body`, `corner`) individually.

## Where the dark theme overrides component defaults

`src/model/Component.ts:164-176`:
```ts
    mergeDefaultAndTheme(option: Opt, ecModel: GlobalModel): void {
        ...
        const themeModel = ecModel.getTheme();
        zrUtil.merge(option, themeModel.get(this.mainType));
        zrUtil.merge(option, this.getDefaultOption());
```
Merge is non-overwriting, so precedence is: user option > theme (`theme[mainType]`, here `theme.matrix`) > `defaultOption`. The theme key must exactly equal the component mainType `'matrix'` (`MatrixModel.type = 'matrix'`, MatrixModel.ts:273) and the sub-keys must exactly match `MatrixOption`.
`src/model/Global.ts:1014-1041` (`mergeTheme`) explicitly skips names registered as component classes (`if (!ComponentModel.hasClass(name))`), so `theme.matrix` is handled only by the path above.
`ThemeOption = Dictionary<any>` (`src/util/types.ts:828`), which is why the bogus keys below compile silently.

## The defective code

`src/theme/dark.ts:56-63`:
```ts
const matrixAxis = {
    label: {
        color: color.secondary
    },
    itemStyle: {
        borderColor: color.neutral20
    }
};
```
`src/theme/dark.ts:187-196`:
```ts
    matrix: {
        x: matrixAxis,
        y: matrixAxis,
        backgroundColor: {
            borderColor: '#817f91'
        },
        innerBackgroundStyle: {
            borderColor: '#484753'
        }
    },
```
Concretely wrong:
1. `backgroundColor` is not a matrix option — the real key is `backgroundStyle` (MatrixOption declared at MatrixModel.ts:43, default at MatrixModel.ts:264). Result: the matrix outer border stays `tokens.color.axisLine` (light-mode `#54555a`, a dark gray) in dark mode.
2. `innerBackgroundStyle` does not exist anywhere in `src/` (verified by grep: zero hits outside this file). Dead option.
3. `body` and `corner` are absent, so body/corner label text stays `tokens.color.secondary` = `#54555a` (near-invisible on the dark background `rgba(2,5,11,1)`) and body cell borders stay `tokens.color.borderTint` = `#cfd2d7` (glaring light gray).
4. `dividerLineStyle` is absent, so the header divider lines stay `tokens.color.border` = `#b7b9be`.
5. Hardcoded hexes instead of `tokens.darkColor` — inconsistent with every other block in this file.

## Exact replacement

Replace `src/theme/dark.ts:56-63` with (keeps the `matrixAxis` name so the `x:`/`y:` references need no rename):
```ts
const matrixAxis = {
    label: {
        color: color.secondary
    },
    itemStyle: {
        borderColor: color.borderTint
    },
    dividerLineStyle: {
        color: color.border
    }
};
const matrixBody = {
    label: {
        color: color.secondary
    },
    itemStyle: {
        borderColor: color.borderTint
    }
};
const matrixCorner = {
    label: {
        color: color.secondary
    }
    // Do not set `itemStyle.borderColor` here: the corner default is 'none'
    // (see `makeDefaultCellItemStyleOption(true)` in MatrixModel.ts), and the
    // theme merge is non-overwriting, so setting it would make dark mode grow
    // corner borders that light mode does not have.
};
```

Replace `src/theme/dark.ts:187-196` with:
```ts
    matrix: {
        x: matrixAxis,
        y: matrixAxis,
        body: matrixBody,
        corner: matrixCorner,
        backgroundStyle: {
            borderColor: color.axisLine
        }
    },
```

Note `color` here is `tokens.darkColor` (`src/theme/dark.ts:21-22`). Resolved values (computed by running `modifyHSL(hex, null, s => s * 0.9, l => 1 - l)`, the transform at `src/visual/tokens.ts:170-186`):
- `color.borderTint` -> `rgba(40,43,48,1)` (inverse of `#cfd2d7`) — identical to the `color.neutral20` used today, since light `borderTint === neutral20`; so swapping `neutral20` -> `borderTint` on x/y is a semantic-only change, zero visual delta, and it makes body match x/y exactly.
- `color.border` -> `rgba(65,67,72,1)` (inverse of `#b7b9be`) — divider lines.
- `color.axisLine` -> `rgba(165,166,171,1)` (inverse of `#54555a`) — outer border; also equals `color.secondary`, the label color, matching the light-mode relationship.
- dark background for contrast sanity: `color.background` -> `rgba(2,5,11,1)`.
